  "findings": [
    "INTRODUCED REGRESSION: all four ind5f_hide_widename_{bare,created}_{legacy,teoz} match Java before and mismatch after, including both library modes. Java paints zero stereotype labels; before paints zero; after paints two \u00abx\u00bb labels and enlarges the vertical allocation. These valid inputs have no runtime failure. The name is wider than the stereotype, isolating the newly introduced height/paint error from an older width error.",
    "Exact cause: Participant.getDisplay checks hiddenPortions before inserting a stereotype; its insertion order depends on stereotypePositionTop. ComponentRoseQueue sends that already-filtered, ordered Display to AbstractTextualComponent and USymbolQueue. The changed Rust render_participant_shape passes raw p.stereotype unconditionally, and the changed Queue measurement adds raw stereotype_height unconditionally. The parser retained a raw stereotype while ignoring hide stereotype, so removing the previous bare-queue paint omission exposes text Java explicitly hides. The source comments conflate the raw field with complete Participant Display.",
    "Complete Display is not yet ported. Multiple stereotypes lose \u00abdurable\u00bb (Java twice, Rust zero); spotted syntax is printed literally as \u00ab(S,#99CCFF)storage\u00bb and loses spot shapes; bottom-position stereotypes remain above names; configured stereotype size and color are not honored (19 versus 14 and #BB2255 versus #000000). CreoleParser expands each Stereotype.getLabels with a stereotype-specific font configuration, unlike the current one-string guillemet reconstruction.",
    "Nested boxes retain missing ancestor/collections text: Java emits \u00abbatch\u00bb twice, Rust zero, and legacy Outer occurs twice versus once. The boxed-figure surcharge change is algebraically unchanged for non-queue kinds. Mixed single-box actor/database/collections controls and no-queue controls match before and after, so no new other-kind regression is demonstrated.",
    "Fresh queue matrix is 14/32 valid whole matches after versus 8/32 before, with 10 recoveries and 4 lost passes. Remaining 18 valid whole failures reject. Multiline and styled stereotype, long width, two-queue, and created/destroy probes do supply bounded positive evidence; they do not waive the losses or remaining failures."
